  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/21-seahorses-and-pipefish/pseudophallus_mindii_en/",
      "html": "<p>Their distribution contains central and tropical South America, where it is found predominantly in freshwater habitats.</p><p>Origin: Central and South America.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/21-seahorses-and-pipefish/pseudophallus_mindii_en/",
      "html": "<p>Adults were caught from estuaries and mangrove areas too, while planktonic juveniles have been collected well offshore at sea.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/21-seahorses-and-pipefish/pseudophallus_mindii_en/",
      "html": "<p>A salt additive is recommended, the aquariums should be well structured with fine-leafed plants and little pieces of bogwood, so that the animals can show their natural behavior.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/21-seahorses-and-pipefish/pseudophallus_mindii_en/",
      "html": "<p>The food supply is for the maintenance of pipefishes particularly of importance. They must be located in the food, best in living food, e.g. water fleas, cyclops, small mosquito larvae and artemia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/21-seahorses-and-pipefish/pseudophallus_mindii_en/",
      "html": "<p>At the best they should only be socialized with really peaceful fish, which do not fight with them for food, because they does not have any self-assertion. As tank mates some invertebrates e.g. shrimps will do fine.</p>"
    }
  ],
